Here's a simple CSS code snippet to customize the font size of the page header with the class `.header`:

```css
.header {
  font-size: 24px; /* You can adjust the size as needed */
}
```

### Explanation:
- `.header` selects the element with the class `header`.
- `font-size: 24px;` changes the font size to 24 pixels. You can replace `24px` with any valid font size value (e.g., `1.5em`, `1.2rem`, `16px`, etc.).

### Optional: Add other styles
If you want to style other properties as well, you can extend the CSS like this:

```css
.header {
  font-size: 24px;
  font-family: 'Segoe UI', Tahoma, Geneva, Verdana, sans-serif;
  color: #333;
  text-align: center;
  margin: 20px 0;
}
```

